      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $C$ be a $\kappa $-compact object of $\calC $, $e_{C}: \calC \rightarrow \hat{\SSet }$ the functor corepresented by $C$, and $e_{F(C)}: \calD \rightarrow \hat{\SSet }$ the functor corepresented by $F(C)$. Since $G$ is a right adjoint to $F$, we have an equivalence $e_{F(C)} = e_{C} \circ G$. Since $e_{C}$ and $G$ are both $\kappa $-continuous, $e_{FC}$ is $\kappa $-continuous. It follows that $F(C)$ is $\kappa $-compact, as desired. 
